    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Checks Heron&#x27;s formula against the shoelace formula, then shows why the arrangement matters: for a thin &quot;needle&quot; triangle the textbook form sqrt(s(s-a)(s-b)(s-c)) loses most of its digits, while Kahan&#x27;s rearrangement stays accurate.">

